# PacketStream

> PacketStream is a residential proxy network powered by real users. These docs cover the residential proxy gateway, the Reseller API, the Search API, the Fetch API, and the MCP server that gives AI agents web search and page reading.

Each docs link below is a Markdown page. Remove `index.md` from a link for the HTML page. All docs pages in one file: https://packetstream.io/llms-full.txt

## Residential proxy docs

- [Quickstart: Make your first residential proxy request](https://packetstream.io/docs/index.md): Connect to PacketStream, verify a residential exit, and choose the right targeting and session behavior for your application.
- [Proxy Endpoints and Authentication](https://packetstream.io/docs/endpoints-authentication/index.md): Choose the PacketStream HTTPS, SOCKS5, or HTTP proxy endpoint and authenticate safely with your username and auth key.
- [Proxy Rotation and Sticky Sessions](https://packetstream.io/docs/rotation-sticky-sessions/index.md): Understand PacketStream's connection-based rotation and use sticky sessions to keep one residential exit for a related workflow.
- [Country Targeting](https://packetstream.io/docs/country-targeting/index.md): Request PacketStream residential exits by ISO two-letter country code and handle unavailable countries without accepting the wrong location.
- [Language Integration Examples](https://packetstream.io/docs/language-integrations/index.md): Connect to PacketStream with cURL, Python Requests, Node.js Undici, Go net/http, or Playwright using authenticated HTTPS proxy configuration.
- [Proxy Troubleshooting](https://packetstream.io/docs/troubleshooting/index.md): Diagnose PacketStream authentication, endpoint, targeting, rotation, sticky-session, TLS, and timeout problems safely.

